  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Middle East Response &#x2013; Ensuring Continuity of Treatment and Essential Services for People Affected by HIV, TB and Malaria in Yemen, Syria, Iraq, Jordan, Lebanon and Palestine.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a continuation of the previous two phases implemented in 2017-2018 and 2019-2021, respectively. It is a multi-country project aiming to deliver continuum of care in challenging operating environments, through provision of essential human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), tuberculosis (TB) and malaria services. The interventions are planned towards addressing the needs of general populations with focus on vulnerable groups including refugees, migrants and internally displaced persons and those in hard-to-reach areas in Syria, Yemen and Iraq. It also includes refugees, migrants and vulnerable populations in Jordan and Lebanon where in the latter is expanded to Palestinian refugees.</narrative>
  </description>
